{"availability":"available","full":"bhouston/three-dlss-nr","name":"three-dlss-nr","description":"A Three.js (TSL / WebGPU) port of OpenDLSS-NR, the open-source reimplementation of NVIDIA's DLSS 5 neural rendering network","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":51,"forks":3,"created":"2026-10-02T14:53:07Z","updated":"2026-10-03T02:16:05Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://three-dlss-nr.ben3d.ca","topics":[],"demo":"https://three-dlss-nr.ben3d.ca/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.673Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.673Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.673Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":20,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.673Z","stars":51,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A port to Three.js (TSL / WebGPU) of OpenDLSS-NR by maan. OpenDLSS-NR is an open-source reimplementation of the network behind NVIDIA's DLSS 5 Neural Rendering. All credit for that reimplementation, its numerics and its documentation belongs to OpenDLSS-NR. This repository ports it to three.js and tracks upstream commit 9d08f41, included as the reference/OpenDLSS-NR submodule. Not affiliated with NVIDIA, and no NVIDIA weights are included (details).","The DLSS 5 neural rendering network, as three.js compute nodes, byte for byte. three-dlss-nr runs the 71-block OpenDLSS-NR network as TSL compute kernels inside a WebGPURenderer, fed straight from your three.js scene with no CPU readback. Every intermediate tensor is byte-identical to the reference WebGPU port.","Synthetic weights: output is not meaningful. The demo in split view on the TSL backend, NR off on the left and NR on on the right. Synthetic weights have the right layout and run the network's real arithmetic, but the image they produce means nothing, hence the red field (why). With a real model directory the right half is the re-rendered head. Head: Lee Perry-Smith, CC BY 3.0 (credits)."],"features":["They prove the port computes the same function as the reference. The port is bit-exact against the reference","They let the whole pipeline run end to end in the tests and in the demo."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhouston/three-dlss-nr/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"29c3a100c38658ee5bf3108d77b1560dd272c1f4671b536407a322b808d50452","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:52.095Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A port to Three.js (TSL / WebGPU) of OpenDLSS-NR by maan. OpenDLSS-NR is an open-source reimplementation of the network behind NVIDIA's DLSS 5 Neural Rendering. All credit for that reimplementation, its numerics and its documentation belongs to OpenDLSS-NR. This repository ports it to three.js and tracks upstream commit 9d08f41, included as the reference/OpenDLSS-NR submodule. Not affiliated with NVIDIA, and no NVIDIA weights are included (details).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhouston/three-dlss-nr/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"29c3a100c38658ee5bf3108d77b1560dd272c1f4671b536407a322b808d50452","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhouston/three-dlss-nr/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:52.096Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T02:16:05Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:45.380Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhouston/three-dlss-nr/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:52.097Z","hash":"29c3a100c38658ee5bf3108d77b1560dd272c1f4671b536407a322b808d50452","originalBytes":22933,"storedBytes":22933,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["reference","network","three-dlss-nr","weights","packages","pnpm","model","tsl","same","gpu","nvidia","port","upstream","opendlss-nr","demo","frame","synthetic","webgpu","backend","head","runs","x512","every","parity","real","three.js","against","docs","nod